{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, a psalm of David. YHWH, You have searched me</b> — This psalm is exceedingly distinguished in the ways of HaShem, and there is no psalm like it in these five books. According to a person's understanding of the ways of HaShem and the ways of the soul, he will reflect on its meanings." "Now I shall expound it briefly, with HaShem's help: <b>You have searched me</b> — in the manner of <b>searcher of the heart and examiner of kidneys</b>; and You are able to know all my secrets."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:03.035922401Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}